{
    "file": "Competency_Based_Interviewing.docx",
    "title": "Competency Based Interviewing",
    "duration": "3 Days",
    "overview": [
        "Competency-based interviewing provides a structured method for assessing whether candidates have demonstrated the behaviors, capabilities, and judgment required for successful performance in a role. Rather than relying on general impressions or hypothetical answers alone, the approach uses evidence from candidates’ past behavior and applies consistent criteria to improve the quality, fairness, and defensibility of selection decisions.",
        "This three-day course equips interviewers with the practical skills required to translate role requirements into competencies, develop behavioral questions, probe effectively, evaluate evidence, take useful interview notes, apply rating standards, reduce bias, and reach evidence-based hiring decisions.",
        "Through interview simulations, question-design exercises, evidence-rating cases, probing practice, and panel decision activities, participants develop a disciplined interviewing approach that supports better candidate comparison while maintaining a professional candidate experience."
    ],
    "audience": [
        "HR managers and specialists, recruitment and talent-acquisition professionals, hiring managers, department heads, supervisors, interview-panel members, HR business partners, and employees involved in candidate assessment, selection, promotion, or internal appointment interviews."
    ],
    "methodology": [
        "The course uses an applied methodology combining short presentations, competency-analysis exercises, behavioral-question design, interview demonstrations, structured probing practice, candidate-response analysis, note-taking exercises, rating and calibration activities, interview simulations, panel decision cases, peer feedback, and action planning."
    ],
    "competencies": [
        "Competency-based interviewing",
        "Behavioral question design",
        "Structured probing",
        "Active listening",
        "Evidence gathering",
        "Candidate assessment",
        "Interview note taking",
        "Behavioral rating",
        "Bias awareness",
        "Selection decision making",
        "Panel interviewing",
        "Professional candidate communication"
    ],
    "objectivesIntro": [
        "By the end of the course, participants will be able to:"
    ],
    "objectives": [
        "Explain the principles and benefits of competency-based interviewing.",
        "Translate job requirements into relevant competencies and behavioral indicators.",
        "Develop structured behavioral questions linked to specific competencies.",
        "Use effective probing techniques to obtain complete and relevant evidence.",
        "Distinguish strong behavioral evidence from vague, theoretical, or unsupported answers.",
        "Take concise interview notes that support objective evaluation.",
        "Apply defined rating criteria consistently across candidates.",
        "Recognize and reduce common interviewer biases.",
        "Conduct professional, legally and ethically appropriate interviews.",
        "Coordinate panel interviews and consolidate evidence fairly.",
        "Make selection recommendations based on demonstrated competency evidence.",
        "Develop a practical competency-based interview structure for future use."
    ],
